My 6th Ascension; my first one with a Valkyrie (others were knight, wizard,
wizard, knight, ranger (genoless!))  My third Valkyrie who was likely to
ascend; I had one escape the dungeon back when I was trying to break the habit
(hah), and the one right before this died of not wearing gloves right after
finding the Vibrating Square, i.e. player stupidity.

I think I started out somewhat reckless, reading scrolls and drinking potions,
and polymorphing from a potion.  At some later point I drank from a fountain
and got a wish, with GDSM.  I got Mjollnir at some decent point and mostly
relied on it.  I got a shield of reflection somewhere and replaced my +3
shield with it, then later found an amulet and started twoweaponing with the
+6 long sword or a +3 silver saber.  I went and killed the Angel who lives
next door to Medusa; usually I leave them alone.  That got me Sunsword, which
I used for a while in Gehennom as a light source and undead-killer --
especially in the Valley.  When I got a (blessed, unrubbed) magic lamp in
Gehennom I went to Mjollnir and silver saber, then Mjollnir and long sword
once I left Hell, and Sunsword and long sword on Astral due to everyone being
shock resistant.

Got crowned of course, and Vorpal Blade, but apart from a Jabberwock or two I
didn't use it.

I noticed that long sword damage seemed to pass through shades; I needed an
artifact or saber to hurt them.

I never found a scroll of magic mapping, but scanning Gehennom for loot was
good for me anyway.  Levitation seemed to take a while to come, but I got
boots eventually -- maybe even near Medusa's Titan.  There was a 'normal'
level' right before the Castle, after the mazes; that was new to me.

IDed a ring of teleport control, then ate a tengu and got control.  Never did
get teleportitis.

Had a ring of conflict, but lost it (unreflected lightning); picked up a spare
on the way up but never used it.  Outside the sanctum I got through most of
the undead stealthily, killing them one by one; then the priests got through
the door and things went haywire.  But I had a drum and beat it a lot to get
the insects to run away.  Drums and tooled horns are a fun reason to play
elven wizards... a wand of SDD made finding the door easy, and the High Priest
died easily.  No one else was in the sanctum or crossed the traps, so I had
time to refresh some spells.

I discovered on the way up that killing the priest in the Valley is murder.
Fortunately I'd left some floating eyes alone just in case I needed a refresher
course.  Of course then I had to find them, but I got one on level 1 or 2.

This Valkyrie, and the one before it, found tons of spellbooks, it was really
disgusting, especially compared to some starved wizards.  Not that I used it a
lot but I did charm monster a few times, and haste self (especially near the
end -- no speed boots) and magic missile; I don't remember much else, although
I knew lots of spells.

I killed some liches and mind flayers, but eventually got worried about
summoning storms and genocided the lot.

Don't remember what I wished for.  GoP, Helm of Brilliance, possibly a ring of
free action, a couple of magic markers, scrolls of charging, scrolls of
genocide... okay, guess I do remember.

My highest level character in a while, if not ever -- 22!  No foocubus sex,
just wraiths and potions of gain level.

Not many scrolls of gold detection, but I had the Orb, so who cares?  Earth was easy, Air not bad when I was very fast -- teleported a few elementals, Fire was the usual no-fight race to the portal, and Water didn't last too long.

Went for Pestilence, as I usually do, and got lucky.  Hmm, looks like it was
coming for me again.

